where is my cumin  it's right here hi guys it's your girl  katura king from masterchef and today  we're going to be talking about how to  cook when you are single we're not  talking about any old takeouts or  deliveries no no no today i'm going to  be showing you how to cook some  delicious delightful and delectable  recipes for breakfast lunch and dinner  because let's face it you are the most  important person in your life you might  as well treat yourself and that's  exactly what we'll be doing today from  the beautiful radisson blue in sunny  dakar senegal let's get to these recipes  this is a dish that i first had when i  went to istanbul turkey and i absolutely  fell in love with it so we start with a  good glug of olive oil and we're going  to render some red onions down in that  saute the onions with some chopped green  peppers one of my favorite things about  metamen is the fact that it reminds me  of a middle eastern shakshuka but with a  fun twist and that is a feta cheese now  any dish that contains cheese has my  heart so you have your onions and  peppers rendering down add some tomatoes  in there i prefer fresh diced tomatoes  so once you have those stewed down add  some seasoning black pepper and salt and  of course some oregano a little known  secret about me is i'm actually a  morning person and i like to start the  day off with a bout of meditation i  listen to some affirmations and then i  start with a very healthy breakfast and  lots of black coffee  to add our whipped eggs in there and you  want to do all of this on a low heat so  it doesn't fry up too quickly when it's  almost finished cooking you add your  cheese in and just sprinkle that all  around i believe that you should  definitely take some time out for  yourself in order to really center  yourself so whether that is literally  just sitting down reading a book or  doing some exercise quickly something  just for you in order to set the tone  for the day once you see that it started  to coagulate if you will then just pull  it off the fire you would probably eat  this with some crusty buttered bread  carbs actually make me very sleepy so i  do not eat carbohydrates in the morning  add some fresh herbs to the side an  additional sprinkle of your pepper i  told you i like things really spicy but  of course this isn't optional and then  some sun-dried tomatoes and there you  have it so let's get into it shall we  that's delicious and i'm not just saying  it because i made it the reason it's one  of my favorite dishes is because it's so  creamy and i find the fact that you  don't have to use any butter or milk in  it just that little touch of feta cheese  makes everything so heavenly all right  guys i will see you around lunchtime  now this time for lunch we're making a  greek pink porn salad it's inspired by a  trip that i took to mykonos i had the  time of my life and one thing that i ate  in abundance was seafood and my absolute  favorite king prawn and this is  something that can easily be substituted  with some shrimp or some salmon you can  actually even substitute it with some  chicken if you wanted to now i've  already de-shelled and de-veined these  beauties i tend to use lemon juice you  can also choose to use lime juice i am  going to add some salt and some garlic  powder into that and you really don't  want to put too much garlic powder  because you find that it will overpower  the seafood let's get the olive oil in  there the pan's been heating up for a  while so you'll find that it cooks very  quickly you want to cook your seafood on  a nice high heat i like to flash fry it  quite quickly because you find that once  you take it out it will still continue  to cook let it really crisp up and firm  up if you're using salmon you want it  skin side down if you are using shrimp  or prawns you can flip that over within  two minutes because we've had it on such  a nice high heat you've got a beautiful  little crust on the outer edges of the  corn i will take that off now whilst i  assemble the ingredients for our salad i  like to use generally a lot of different  types of lettuce just to give it a bit  of body use whatever lettuce you can  find so i just rip that up i like to  engage in a lot of self  and some ways that i engage in self-love  i tend to take a nap during the  afternoon being like woken up quite  early in the daytime take that siesta  make sure you revive yourself so let's  get the rest of this salad prepped up we  have some cherry tomatoes that we'll be  adding in there i like to add some red  roasted bell peppers so it adds a little  smoky flavor profile to your salad my  favorite avocado and then we'll add some  fresh red onions in there for a bit of  crunch you don't want to add too much  because let's face it nobody likes onion  breath in the middle of the day add some  cucumbers and next up we're going to add  a grecian favorite of course some olives  now even though you're cooking for  yourself presentation still matters now  for the vinaigrette i like a very heavy  sichuan base a nice little citrus flavor  profile to it so i use not just lemon  juice but also lemon zest that's my  little cheat sheet i add some oregano in  there some dried oregano garlic powder  black pepper let's add some sea salt in  there now this reminds me of one of my  favorite vinaigrettes one of the  dressings that i had whilst i was in  greece one of my favorite things to do  is travel solo it really just brings a  certain sense of self that you don't  experience when you're traveling with  other people i know travel's hard right  now but once the world opens back up do  not be afraid to travel while you're  single so we'll add some dijon mustard  into the base so just whisk your  vinaigrette and so here's the  consistency that you're looking for not  as viscous as perhaps a syrup but  definitely a lot thicker than water  let's say pour that over your salad and  then i like to build it up with a little  more fresh vegetables so we'll add a few  more cherry tomatoes to the top of that  where would we be without our feta  cheese our trusty feta and then you top  it up with our favorite there you have  your wonderful grecian salad nice  luxurious simple healthy flavors can't  wait to dive in  i know you can't taste it but you guys  need to recreate this dish and let me  know exactly what you think this tastes  absolutely divine but i am knackered so  i'm gonna go and have a siesta and i'll  see you guys back here for dinner  okay guys now it's time for our  wonderful dinner preparation and today  i'm making an amazingly authentic  senegalese yasapuli now yasser filet is  one of the best chicken dishes you will  ever have and one of the things that i  love about all the dishes that we've  created today is the fact that they use  very similar ingredients not only do you  get to save on your grocery shopping but  you also get to utilize all of the  things in your pantry so let's get to  the yasa pulae shall we get a chicken  thigh or chicken lab and i like to  generally marinate the chicken with the  yatsapulu marinade overnight if you  don't remember to marinate it the night  before you can always do it two or three  hours prior to creating your dish i like  to score the chicken so you have tasty  skin and also you've got very aromatic  meat as well first things first i'm  going to use a west african maggie brian  q it's west african only because it's  something that we generally use quite a  lot as the base of our dishes in west  africa but you can easily find this in  any supermarket around the world so just  crumble those up add some dried oregano  some black pepper the exact same amount  of white pepper some garlic powder then  i also like to use some fresh garlic and  there are three stars to the show here  the acids in the form of both lemon and  vinegar so i add some zest in there some  fresh lemon juice your secondary acid  which is your vinegar and then we're  going to add dijon mustard and then add  your white onions in so you want the  onions thinly sliced add a bay leaf and  the fun begins now with this you really  gotta get right in there and marinate  and massage your chicken and then we pop  that in the fridge and let it rest for  about two to three hours or preferably  overnight so i have this chicken that i  marinated overnight but we are going to  cook the two together today the  traditional way of making yasakule is to  grill the chicken beforehand to ensure  that you have a nice crust on the  outside in the absence of a grill you  can pan fry it a nice healthy glove of  olive oil in your pan  and your pan has been preheated so it is  going to smoke up very quickly and you  want to get the chicken in skin side  down so we're going to cook each side of  the chicken for about 5-10 minutes on a  very high heat until you see it start to  crust up and become a nice golden brown  so what we're going to do next is add  some water in and let that chicken and  sauce really just simmer and stew you're  going to reduce that fire that you  previously had on a very high heat down  to a low to medium heat add one whole  scotch bunnet in there for those of you  that don't like a lot of heat this is  perfect because you're not exposing the  seeds and that's where all the spice  really is so we're gonna let that simmer  for about 15 to 20 minutes or until it  reaches an internal temperature of about  165 while you move on to making your  accompaniment you can have a green salad  i like to opt for a nice crisp carrot  salad so you add a pinch of cumin in  there our trusty lemon zest some fresh  lemon juice pinch of sea salt and your  olive oil i also like to take some basil  or parsley leaves and slightly bruise  them in the hands chop them up very  roughly put that in there for color and  of course for flavor mix that all up and  that is your very simple side carrot  salad and it's time for us to check and  see if our chicken is ready now what  you're looking for is for the sauce to  reduce down and sort of thickened up and  that is exactly  what we have and what you want to do now  that it's ready to serve is get some  pre-boiled white rice so you want to  serve your chicken thigh over the rice  and then add these juicy onions and if  you like additional heat then you can  take one of the scotch bonnets that you  put in there pop it on the top like so  add your carrot salad to the side and i  like to add some additional fresh herbs  on top so we'll add some additional  color in the form of our char grilled  peppers from earlier and there you have  your traditional senegalese yasakuli  this looks absolutely beautiful so let's  check in to this delectable senegalese  dish  okay  that is good one thing i love about  senegal is the fact that they know food  very simple ingredients but full of  flavor those flavors really burst in  your mouth well that's all for me today  i hope you've enjoyed this trip around  the world from the comfort of your  kitchen i really hope that you do  recreate these dishes and if you do  please be sure to tag me and to all my  single ladies and single men out there  make sure that you love on yourselves i  know these are very strange times that  we're all going through but be sure to  take the time out for yourself each and  every day and remember that you are the  most special person that you will ever  meet bye  [Music]  you

